<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>This import is verified by the signature step of the download recipe (AuthenticodeVerifier: a valid, timestamped signature of the Scratch Foundation under a pinned root), so a real run needs only the dry-run switch of the override. Without that step the shared importer refuses a real run unless the override sets pcman_allow_unverified to true (the run then publishes with a WARNING, and the report says published, NOT verified). Hands the downloaded Scratch 3 installer (an EXE) to the package tool (pcman), which publishes it as a new version of the template item into the Cimian repository, or says that nothing is new. For an EXE the package tool is given the version label: the recipe passes the version that the download recipe's WindowsExeVersion step read from the signed file's own version resource, after it checked that the resource names the product Scratch 3 of the company Scratch Foundation and that the version equals the one in the file name that the redirect names (3.32.1 on 2026-11-13). Whether the version that the installed program reports is the same is NOT established, and whether the package tool checks that an EXE is the same product as the template was NOT established. Whether the installer installs for the whole machine when the client runs it as SYSTEM is NOT established either. This is a dry run, which writes nothing, until the recipe's override sets pcman_dry_run to false.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.pcman.Scratch</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>Scratch</string>
            <key>PCMAN_TEMPLATE</key>
            <string>scratch</string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>ParentRecipe</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.Scratch-Win</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.PcmanProcessors/PcmanImporter</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>pathname</key>
                    <string>%pathname%</string>
                    <key>pcman_template</key>
                    <string>%PCMAN_TEMPLATE%</string>
                    <key>pcman_version</key>
                    <string>%version%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
